<title>SOUTH KOREA: Trading in OB, Doo San Beverage halted.</title>
<headline>Trading in OB, Doo San Beverage halted.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in shares of OB Brewery Co and Doo San Beverage Co was suspended for Tuesday's afternoon session following the announcement of a plan by OB Brewery to absorb Doo San, the Korea Stock Exchange said.  </p>
<p>Trading of their shares will resume on Wednesday morning, an exchange official said.</p>
<p>A statement released by the Securities Supervisory Board said earlier on Tuesday OB Brewery had decided to absorb its sister firm Doo San Beverage on October 1.</p>
<p>OB Brewery shares closed Tuesday's morning session 2,300 won lower at 31,000 won and Doo San shares were 900 won higher at 34,700 won.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
